# Everything normalizes to LF in the repo, checked out per-platform...
* text=auto

# ...except EDI files, where line endings are DATA, not formatting.
#
# A segment's leading whitespace round-trips through parse()/serialize()
# byte for byte, and the parity suite asserts it. Letting git rewrite the
# line endings on checkout would silently change fixture content and break
# that guarantee, so these are excluded from all EOL normalization.
#
# These MUST stay below `* text=auto`: in .gitattributes the LAST matching
# rule wins, so with the catch-all last it silently overrode these and the
# exemption did nothing. Verify with:
#
#   git check-attr -a web/tests/samples/tree/cob_loops.edi   # -> text: unset
*.edi -text
*.txt -text
